  "description": "Every frame the device login adds to the session stream: four from the client (`device_login_attach`, `device_login_hostkey_answer`, `device_login_answer`, `device_login_cancel`) and three from the server (`device_login_hostkey`, `device_login_prompt` in its three methods, `device_login_result`), each with a valid instance and an invalid one. Each is additive: every frame keeps v 1, and a peer that predates the device login ignores a `t` it does not know (V1). `device_login_prompt` is a closed `oneOf` over `method`: `banner` carries only `text`; `password` carries `attempt` and `prompt_id` and no device text; `keyboard-interactive` carries `attempt`, `name`, `instruction` and `prompts`, and `prompt_id` exactly when `prompts` is not empty. A consumer that meets a `method` or a hostkey `kind` it does not know sends `device_login_cancel` and says it is too old for this device login, and never offers Accept for an unknown `kind`; an unknown `outcome` is a failed device login (V5). `answers` holds 1 to 16 strings of 0 to 1024 characters, and an empty string is an answer. A fixture holds no empty answer, because every string under `answers` must be the synthetic constant; the contract's tests hold it.",
  "corpus": [
    "open_decisions §5",
    "credential §10.1",
    "Contract §6",
    "device-login steps 8 to 21",
    "conventions V1, V5, V10",
    "frontend §10.4"
  ],
